{"lines": ["Go back to Hopkinsville. The family said the creatures stood two to four feet tall, with glowing eyes, at the doors and windows.", "Police were called. Four city officers, five state troopers, three sheriff's deputies, and four military police from Fort Campbell all came out.", "They found no creatures. They found broken windows, and holes in the window screens.", "The family said the things came back around three thirty in the morning. Then they left.", "Now the size. The skeptic Brian Dunning points out that a great horned owl stands about two thirds of a metre tall. It is nocturnal, it flies silently, it has yellow eyes, and it will defend its nest.", "That matches two to four feet better than you might expect.", "Dunning adds that a luminous patch reported at the scene is consistent with foxfire, a glowing fungus.", "Rule three. Before you decide what it is, measure it against what lives there. Height, wingspan, eyes. The real list of local animals is shorter than your imagination."], "words": [["Go", 0.0, 0.14], ["back", 0.14, 0.42], ["to", 0.42, 0.62], ["Hopkinsville.", 0.62, 1.36], ["The", 1.78, 1.9], ["family", 1.9, 2.16], ["said", 2.16, 2.58], ["the", 2.58, 2.7], ["creatures", 2.7, 3.0], ["stood", 3.0, 3.44], ["two", 3.44, 3.76], ["to", 3.76, 3.9], ["four", 3.9, 4.22], ["feet", 4.22, 4.52], ["tall,", 4.52, 4.84], ["with", 4.84, 5.16], ["glowing", 5.16, 5.4], ["eyes,", 5.4, 5.94], ["at", 5.94, 6.3], ["the", 6.3, 6.42], ["doors", 6.42, 6.72], ["and", 6.72, 7.0], ["windows.", 7.0, 7.32], ["Police", 8.16, 8.66], ["were", 8.66, 8.92], ["called.", 8.92, 9.24], ["Four", 9.7, 9.86], ["city", 9.86, 10.2], ["officers,", 10.2, 10.64], ["five", 11.14, 11.38], ["state", 11.38, 11.74], ["troopers,", 11.74, 12.06], ["three", 12.56, 12.72], ["sheriff's", 12.72, 13.32], ["deputies,", 13.32, 13.48], ["and", 14.04, 14.09], ["four", 14.09, 14.4], ["military", 14.4, 14.76], ["police", 14.76, 15.24], ["from", 15.24, 15.62], ["Fort", 15.62, 15.84], ["Campbell", 15.84,